IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ta-dates`
IMPORT `ta-rules`

-- Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) -- the questions of the BENEFICIARY.
--
-- SEAT: the individual for whom property is held on trust: a beneficiary of a private trust or of a deceased estate, and
-- in particular a child or an adult under a disability whose compensation or damages are held on trust for them (asking
-- through a parent, guardian or administrator where they cannot ask themselves). "Can my trustee invest in this?", "What
-- standard must my trustee meet?", "Has my trustee reviewed the investments in time?", "Can money be used for my
-- maintenance while I am under 18?", "Must the income be paid to me now I am 18?", "How much of my capital can be
-- advanced to me?", "Whose consent is needed before property is appropriated to my share?", "Who can replace my
-- trustee?", "Can the Court make orders for my property, vary my trust, or excuse my trustee?", "What happens if my
-- trustee ignores my written direction?". The trustee, the Court and State Trustees get no seat: the trustee's and the
-- Court's judgments are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers in dollars, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of
-- ta-rules.l4. The two duties with deadlines (ss 6(3), 51(2)(i)) are DEONTIC rules run inside; no question takes a
-- DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Trustee Act
-- 1958, Version No. 127 (1 September 2023), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the
-- authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the
-- Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Trustee Act 1958: the beneficiary's questions`

§§ `Which court`

@export Which court can make orders about my trust property under the Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) (s 3)? The Supreme Court always; the County Court too where the property's value is within its jurisdictional limit. Payments into court go to the Supreme Court only (s 69(7)).
GIVEN `is the value within the County Court limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the value of the trust property concerned does not exceed the County Court's jurisdictional limit (set by the County Court Act 1958)
GIVETH A `The Court for my trust`
`Which court can deal with my trust` MEANS
    `s 3 -- the Court` `is the value within the County Court limit`

§§ `How my trustee invests (Part I)`

@export May my trustee invest the trust money in this investment, or change an investment (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 5)? A trustee may invest in any form of investment and vary investments at any time, unless the trust instrument expressly prohibits it.
GIVEN `does the instrument prohibit it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will, deed or order creating your trust expressly prohibits this investment or this kind of investment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my trustee make this investment` MEANS
    `s 5 -- the trustee may invest in it` `does the instrument prohibit it`

@export What standard of care, diligence and skill must my trustee use when investing the trust money (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 6(1))? A professional trustee or investor is held to the standard of a prudent professional; anyone else to that of a prudent person managing other people's affairs.
GIVEN `is investing or trusteeship my trustee's work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your trustee's profession, business or employment is or includes acting as a trustee or investing money for other people (for example a trustee company, State Trustees, a lawyer or financial adviser acting as trustee)
      `does the instrument set another standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will, deed or order creating your trust sets a different standard of care for investing (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Standard of care in investing`
`What standard must my trustee meet when investing` MEANS
    `s 6(1) -- the standard of care` `is investing or trusteeship my trustee's work` `does the instrument set another standard`

@export Must my trustee obtain a consent or approval before making trust investments (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 6(2))? Yes, where a binding provision of the trust instrument requires one.
GIVEN `does the instrument require a consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will, deed or order creating your trust requires someone's consent or approval for trust investments
      `does that provision bind the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that provision is binding on your trustee
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my trustee get consent before investing` MEANS
    `s 6(2) -- the trustee must obtain the consent` `does the instrument require a consent` `does that provision bind the trustee`

@export Has my trustee reviewed the performance of the trust investments in time (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 6(3))? A trustee must review them, one by one and as a whole, at least once in each year; read here as within a year of the last review.
GIVEN `the day of the last review` IS A DATE @desc The day your trustee last reviewed the trust investments (or, if never, the day the trust money was first invested)
      `has the trustee reviewed since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your trustee has reviewed the investments again since that day
      `the day of the next review` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day of that next review (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `does the instrument provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will, deed or order creating your trust provides otherwise about reviewing investments (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE `What became of the duty`
`Has my trustee reviewed the investments in time` MEANS
    `s 6(3) -- what became of the yearly review` `the day of the last review` `has the trustee reviewed since` `the day of the next review` `today` `does the instrument provide otherwise`

@export Must my trustee consider this matter when investing the trust money (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 8(1))? The trustee must have regard to each of fifteen matters so far as appropriate to the trust, among them the beneficiaries' needs, diversification, risk, inflation, liquidity, tax and costs.
GIVEN `which matter` IS AN `Investment matter` @desc The matter you are asking about, one of the fifteen in section 8(1)(a) to (o)
      `is it appropriate to my trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter is appropriate to the circumstances of your trust (for a child's compensation fund, for example, the child's needs and the fund's likely duration)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my trustee consider this matter when investing` MEANS
    `s 8(1) -- the trustee must have regard to the matter` `which matter` `is it appropriate to my trust`

@export Can my trustee pay for investment advice out of the trust money (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) ss 7(4), 8(2))? Reasonable costs of independent, impartial advice reasonably required from an adviser the trustee reasonably believes competent, or of advice the trustee had a duty to take, may be paid from the trust.
GIVEN `did the trustee have a duty to take this advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the general law put your trustee under a duty to take this advice (answer no if unsure)
      `is the advice independent and impartial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the advice is independent and impartial (the adviser is not selling the investment, for example)
      `was the advice reasonably required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the advice was reasonably required for investing the trust money or managing the investments
      `does the trustee reasonably believe the adviser competent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your trustee reasonably believes the adviser is competent to give the advice
      `are the costs reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cost of the advice is reasonable
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the cost of investment advice come out of my trust` MEANS
    `ss 7(4), 8(2) -- the advice may be paid for out of trust funds` `did the trustee have a duty to take this advice` `is the advice independent and impartial` `was the advice reasonably required` `does the trustee reasonably believe the adviser competent` `are the costs reasonable`

@export May my trustee buy a home for me to live in, arrange one for me, or keep one the trust holds for me (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 11)? Buying or arranging is allowed unless the trust instrument forbids it; keeping one is allowed despite the instrument if it would not unfairly prejudice the other beneficiaries.
GIVEN `which arrangement` IS A `Home for a beneficiary` @desc What the trustee would do: buy a dwelling house for you to live in, make another arrangement giving you a right to live in one, or keep one the trust already holds for you to live in
      `does the instrument forbid it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will, deed or order creating your trust forbids it (answer no if unsure)
      `would it unfairly prejudice the others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it would unfairly prejudice the interests of the trust's other beneficiaries
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my trustee provide a home for me` MEANS
    `s 11 -- the trustee may provide the home` `which arrangement` `does the instrument forbid it` `would it unfairly prejudice the others`

§§ `When my trustee answers for a loss on an investment (Part I)`

@export Can I hold my trustee liable just because it kept an investment that is no longer authorised or proper (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 12)? No: keeping it is not by itself a breach of trust. Other complaints about the investment are not answered here.
GIVEN `has the investment ceased to be authorised or proper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the investment has ceased to be one authorised by the trust instrument, by law, or properly made
      `is keeping it my only complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your only complaint is that the trustee kept it (not, for example, that it was imprudent to keep)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my trustee liable just for keeping the investment` MEANS
    `s 12 -- the trustee is liable for keeping the investment` `has the investment ceased to be authorised or proper` `is keeping it my only complaint`

@export Is my trustee protected from liability for lending too much of the trust money against a property, because it relied on a valuation (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 12A)? Yes, if the trustee acted on an independent valuer's report it reasonably believed competent and lent no more than two-thirds of the reported value.
GIVEN `the loan` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of trust money lent, in dollars
      `the value in the report` IS A NUMBER @desc The property's value as stated in the valuation report, in dollars
      `did the trustee act on a valuation report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee, in making the loan, acted on a report on the property's value
      `did the trustee reasonably believe the valuer competent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee reasonably believed the valuer competent to give the report
      `was the valuer instructed independently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee instructed and employed the valuer independently of any owner of the property
      `was the loan made relying on the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loan was made in reliance on the report
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my trustee protected for the amount lent on a valuation` MEANS
    `s 12A -- the trustee is protected as to the proportion lent` `the loan` `the value in the report` `did the trustee act on a valuation report` `did the trustee reasonably believe the valuer competent` `was the valuer instructed independently` `was the loan made relying on the report`

@export How much must my trustee make good for advancing too much trust money on a security that would have been proper for a smaller sum (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 12B)? Only the excess over the smaller sum, with interest.
GIVEN `the sum advanced` IS A NUMBER @desc The trust money actually advanced on the security, in dollars
      `the smaller proper sum` IS A NUMBER @desc The largest sum for which the security would have been a proper investment at the time, in dollars
      `the interest on the difference` IS A NUMBER @desc The interest on the excess, in dollars (the Act does not state the rate)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much must my trustee make good for advancing too much` MEANS
    `s 12B -- the most the trustee must make good` `the sum advanced` `the smaller proper sum` `the interest on the difference`

@export In my claim against my trustee for a loss on an investment, can the Court set gains on other investments off against the loss (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 12D)?
GIVEN `is it an action for breach of trust over an investment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is an action for breach of trust arising out of an investment the trustee made
      `has the trust lost or will it lose money on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trust has sustained, or is expected to sustain, a loss on that investment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Court set gains off against the loss` MEANS
    `s 12D -- the Court may set off gains against the loss` `is it an action for breach of trust over an investment` `has the trust lost or will it lose money on it`

@export Is my trustee protected from liability for the proportion lent on a home loan made from the trust money, because the loan was insured (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 12E)? Yes, if the trust did not forbid lending on real security, the loan was a housing loan, and it is insured in the prescribed form with an authorised insurer.
GIVEN `was the trustee forbidden to lend on real security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trust instrument expressly forbade the trustee to lend money on a real security (a mortgage of land)
      `the purpose of the loan` IS A `Purpose of the loan` @desc What the loan was for, one of the six housing purposes in section 12E(6) (buying land and building a home, building, buying land with a home, altering or extending, roads and footpaths, discharging a mortgage during building) or none
      `is it secured over the borrower's land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether repayment is secured over the borrower's interest in the land
      `is it insured with an authorised insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loan is secured by a contract of insurance in the prescribed form with an insurer the Minister has declared authorised
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my trustee protected for an insured home loan` MEANS
    `s 12E -- the trustee is protected as to the proportion lent on a housing loan` `was the trustee forbidden to lend on real security` `the purpose of the loan` `is it secured over the borrower's land` `is it insured with an authorised insurer`

§§ `Selling, mortgaging and insuring trust property (Part II Division 1)`

@export If I ask in writing, may my trustee sell trust property under a power of sale even though time has passed or all the beneficiaries are absolutely entitled (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 14)? Yes, where the power's duration is not expressly limited. It is a power, not a duty to sell.
GIVEN `is there a power to sell` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trust instrument gives a power to sell the property
      `does the instrument limit how long the power lasts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the instrument expressly limits how long the power to sell lasts
      `have I or another beneficiary asked in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or another beneficiary has asked the trustee in writing to sell
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my trustee sell at my written request` MEANS
    `s 14 -- the trustee may sell at a beneficiary's written request` `is there a power to sell` `does the instrument limit how long the power lasts` `have I or another beneficiary asked in writing`

@export Can I challenge my trustee's sale because the conditions of sale were unnecessarily depreciatory (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 15)? Only if they made the price inadequate; and after the conveyance, not against the purchaser unless the purchaser colluded with the trustee.
GIVEN `were the conditions unnecessarily depreciatory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any condition of sale was unnecessarily depreciatory (lowering what buyers would pay, for example a needless restriction on title)
      `did they make the price inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those conditions made the price inadequate
      `has the conveyance been executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer to the purchaser has been signed (executed)
      `did the purchaser collude with the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the purchaser was acting in collusion with the trustee when the contract of sale was made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I challenge the sale for depreciatory conditions` MEANS
    `s 15 -- the sale may be impeached for depreciatory conditions` `were the conditions unnecessarily depreciatory` `did they make the price inadequate` `has the conveyance been executed` `did the purchaser collude with the trustee`

@export On selling trust land, may my trustee leave part of the price owing on a mortgage of the land sold (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 16)? Up to three-fifths of the price, where the proceeds are to be invested; on a sale under a Court order, only as the Court directs.
GIVEN `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The purchase price of the land, in dollars
      `the part left on mortgage` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of the price to be secured by a mortgage of the land sold, in dollars
      `are the proceeds to be invested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sale proceeds are liable to be invested under the trust
      `is it a sale under a Court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sale is made under an order of the Court
      `has the Court directed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the Court has directed that part of the price may be left on mortgage
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my trustee leave part of the price on mortgage` MEANS
    `s 16 -- the trustee may leave part of the price on mortgage` `the price` `the part left on mortgage` `are the proceeds to be invested` `is it a sale under a Court order` `has the Court directed it`

@export Do the terms of my trustee's sale of trust land on deferred payment meet the Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) minimums (s 17(3))? A deposit of at least one-tenth and at least what a prudent owner would accept; interest at least half-yearly; the whole price within ten years; the whole due after at most six months in arrears; and the buyer to maintain and insure the property.
GIVEN `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The purchase price, in dollars
      `the deposit` IS A NUMBER @desc The deposit the terms require, in dollars
      `the prudent deposit` IS A NUMBER @desc The deposit a person acting with prudence would, if the land were their own, have accepted to sell it to best advantage, in dollars
      `months between interest payments` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months apart interest on the unpaid balance is payable
      `years until the whole price is due` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years from the date of sale until the whole price must be paid
      `months in arrears before the whole price falls due` IS A NUMBER @desc After how many months of an instalment or interest being in arrears the whole price becomes due
      `must the buyer maintain and insure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the terms require the buyer to maintain and protect the property and insure any buildings against fire to full insurable value
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Do the deferred payment terms meet the minimums` MEANS
    `s 17(3) -- the deferred payment terms meet the minimums` `the price` `the deposit` `the prudent deposit` `months between interest payments` `years until the whole price is due` `months in arrears before the whole price falls due` `must the buyer maintain and insure`

@export Once land has been sold on deferred payment, may my trustee now transfer it to the buyer and take a mortgage back for the balance (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 17(4))? Only after two-fifths of the price has been paid.
GIVEN `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The purchase price, in dollars
      `the amount paid so far` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the price the buyer has paid so far, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my trustee transfer the land and take a mortgage back` MEANS
    `s 17(4) -- the trustee may convey and take a mortgage back` `the price` `the amount paid so far`

@export May my trustee insure trust property for this amount (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 23)? A trustee may insure against any risk a prudent person would insure against, for any amount, but all insurance together must not exceed the insurable value or liability. Premiums come first out of the property's income.
GIVEN `the new insurance` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the new insurance, in dollars
      `the insurance already in place` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of insurance already in place on the same property or liability, in dollars
      `the insurable value` IS A NUMBER @desc The insurable value of the property, or the amount of the liability, in dollars
      `would a prudent person insure against it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a risk or liability against which it would be prudent for a person acting for themself to insure
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my trustee insure for this amount` MEANS
    `s 23 -- the trustee may insure for the amount` `the new insurance` `the insurance already in place` `the insurable value` `would a prudent person insure against it`

@export Is my trustee shielded by the Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) from answering for this loss to the trust (ss 28(1), 36(1))? A trustee answers only for its own acts, receipts, neglects and defaults: not for another trustee, a banker or depositary, a good-faith agent, insufficient securities, or receipts signed only for conformity, unless the loss came through its own wilful default.
GIVEN `what caused the loss` IS A `Cause of the loss` @desc What caused the loss: the trustee's own act or default, another trustee's, a banker or other depositary's, an agent's, the insufficiency of securities, a receipt signed for conformity, or something else
      `was it the trustee's own wilful default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loss happened through your trustee's own wilful default (a deliberate or reckless failure in its duty)
      `was the agent employed in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If an agent caused it, whether your trustee employed the agent in good faith
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my trustee shielded from this loss` MEANS
    `ss 28, 36 -- the trustee is shielded from the loss` `what caused the loss` `was it the trustee's own wilful default` `was the agent employed in good faith`

§§ `Appropriating property to my share (s 31)`

@export Before my trustee appropriates trust property to my share, is a consent for my share needed (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 31(5) to (9))? Usually yes; not where the property is an authorised investment and no one can consent for me (a minor with no parent or guardian, an incapable person with no one empowered, a person who cannot be found) and the share has no separate trustee, nor for an annuity fund invested in Commonwealth securities giving at least 120% of the annuity.
GIVEN `my interest` IS A `My interest in the share` @desc Your interest: absolutely entitled to the share now, entitled to the income of a settled share, or an annuitant whose annuity a fund is set apart to pay
      `my standing` IS A `My standing for consent` @desc Whether you are of full age and capacity, a minor, incapable of managing your own affairs, or someone the trustee cannot find or does not know to be alive
      `do I have a parent or guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a minor, whether you have a parent you live with or who has custody of you, or a guardian
      `can someone consent for me by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are incapable of managing your affairs, whether someone (an administrator, for example) has power by law to give the consent for you
      `is it an authorised investment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property appropriated is an investment authorised by law or by the trust instrument
      `does my share have a separate trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your share has its own trustee, other than the trustee making the appropriation
      `the yearly annuity` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are an annuitant, your annuity a year, in dollars (0 if not)
      `the yearly income at par` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the income a year the fund would give if invested in Commonwealth Government securities at par, in dollars (0 if not)
      `is the fund so invested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the fund is actually invested in such securities
      `must the trustee also pay tax on the annuity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the trustee must pay or provide tax or other money in addition to the annuity
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is a consent for my share needed` MEANS
    `s 31 -- a consent for my share is needed` `my interest` `my standing` `do I have a parent or guardian` `can someone consent for me by law` `is it an authorised investment` `does my share have a separate trustee` (`s 31(9) -- the annuitant's consent is not necessary` `the yearly annuity` `the yearly income at par` `is the fund so invested` `must the trustee also pay tax on the annuity`)

@export Who may give the consent before my trustee appropriates trust property to my share (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 31(5) to (7))? The separate trustee of a settled share; you in writing if of full age and capacity; for a minor a parent or guardian, or the Court; for an incapable person whoever has power by law, or the Court; for someone who cannot be found, the Court. Any one listed may consent.
GIVEN `my interest` IS A `My interest in the share` @desc Your interest: absolutely entitled to the share now, entitled to the income of a settled share, or an annuitant whose annuity a fund is set apart to pay
      `my standing` IS A `My standing for consent` @desc Whether you are of full age and capacity, a minor, incapable of managing your own affairs, or someone the trustee cannot find or does not know to be alive
      `does my share have a separate trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your share has its own trustee, other than the trustee making the appropriation
GIVETH A LIST OF `Who may consent`
`Who may consent for my share` MEANS
    `s 31 -- who may consent for my share` `my interest` `my standing` `does my share have a separate trustee`

@export May my trustee appropriate this trust property to my share (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 31(1))? Not so as to prejudice a specific gift, and only with any consent section 31 requires.
GIVEN `would it prejudice a specific gift` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the appropriation would prejudicially affect a specific gift (a particular item left to someone)
      `is a consent needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether section 31 requires a consent for your share (ask the question above)
      `has it been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that consent has been given
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my trustee appropriate this property to my share` MEANS
    `s 31(1) -- the trustee may appropriate the property to my share` `would it prejudice a specific gift` `is a consent needed` `has it been given`

§§ `Notice to claimants before distribution (s 33)`

@export After advertising for claims, is the trustee or executor shielded from my claim to property it has distributed (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 33)? Yes, if the notices were properly advertised, gave at least two months for claims, the distribution came after the day fixed, and it had no notice of my claim. You may still follow the property into the hands of anyone but a purchaser (s 33(3)(a)).
GIVEN `the day of the last notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the last notice to claimants was published
      `the day fixed for claims` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice fixed by which claims had to be sent
      `the day of the distribution` IS A DATE @desc The day the trustee or executor distributed or conveyed the property
      `were the notices properly advertised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notices were advertised as section 33 requires (Government Gazette and a Melbourne daily newspaper, and a local paper for land more than 80 km from Melbourne; for estates of $2000 or less, or State Trustees' elections, one Melbourne daily and a local paper)
      `did they know of my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee or executor had notice of your claim, formal or not, when it distributed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the trustee shielded from my claim after the notice` MEANS
    `s 33 -- the trustee is shielded from my claim` `the day of the last notice` `the day fixed for claims` `the day of the distribution` `were the notices properly advertised` `did they know of my claim`

§§ `Money for me while I am under 18, and when I turn 18 (s 37)`

@export While I am under 18, may my trustee pay or use the income of my trust property for my maintenance, education, advancement or benefit (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 37(1)(a))? Yes, at the trustee's discretion and as is reasonable, paid to my parent or guardian or applied for me, while my interest lasts.
GIVEN `my day of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `does my interest continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your interest in the property still continues (it has not ended or been defeated)
      `the day the instrument came into operation` IS A DATE @desc The day the will, deed or order under which your interest arises came into operation (a will: the day the testator died)
      `is my interest contingent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your interest is contingent (depends on something that may not happen, such as reaching an age)
      `does the gift carry the income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If contingent, whether the gift carries the intermediate income (the income earned before the interest vests)
      `does the instrument say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will, deed or order expresses a contrary intention about using income for your maintenance (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my trustee use the income for me while I am under 18` MEANS
    `s 37(1)(a) -- the trustees may use the income for my maintenance` `my day of birth` `today` `does my interest continue` (`s 37 -- the section can apply to my interest` `the day the instrument came into operation` `is my interest contingent` `does the gift carry the income` `does the instrument say otherwise`)

@export Now that I am 18 but my interest has not vested, must my trustee pay me the income of my trust property (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 37(1)(b))? Yes, until the interest vests, fails, or I die.
GIVEN `my day of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `do I have a vested interest in the income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you already have a vested (unconditional) interest in the income
      `has my interest failed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your interest has failed (for example a condition can no longer be met)
      `the day the instrument came into operation` IS A DATE @desc The day the will, deed or order under which your interest arises came into operation (a will: the day the testator died)
      `is my interest contingent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your interest is contingent (depends on something that may not happen, such as reaching an age)
      `does the gift carry the income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If contingent, whether the gift carries the intermediate income
      `does the instrument say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will, deed or order expresses a contrary intention (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my trustee pay me the income now I am 18` MEANS
    `s 37(1)(b) -- the trustees must pay me the income` `my day of birth` `today` `do I have a vested interest in the income` `has my interest failed` (`s 37 -- the section can apply to my interest` `the day the instrument came into operation` `is my interest contingent` `does the gift carry the income` `does the instrument say otherwise`)

@export What happens to the income accumulated for me while I was under 18 (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 37(2))? It is mine absolutely if my interest in the income was vested, or I became absolutely entitled to the property at 18 or on marriage; otherwise it is added to the capital.
GIVEN `my day of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `did I marry under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you married before turning 18
      `was my interest in the income vested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your interest in the income during your minority (or until marriage) was a vested interest
      `did I become entitled to the property itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at 18 or on marrying under 18, you became entitled to the property itself absolutely (or in fee simple or for an entailed interest)
      `the day the instrument came into operation` IS A DATE @desc The day the will, deed or order under which your interest arises came into operation
      `is my interest contingent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your interest is contingent
      `does the gift carry the income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If contingent, whether the gift carries the intermediate income
      `does the instrument say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will, deed or order expresses a contrary intention (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE `What becomes of the accumulations`
`What happens to the income saved for me while under 18` MEANS
    `s 37(2) -- what becomes of the accumulated income` `my day of birth` `today` `did I marry under 18` `was my interest in the income vested` `did I become entitled to the property itself` (`s 37 -- the section can apply to my interest` `the day the instrument came into operation` `is my interest contingent` `does the gift carry the income` `does the instrument say otherwise`)

@export How much interest a year does my parent's legacy to me carry for my maintenance (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 37(3))? Five per cent a year of the legacy, where a parent (or someone in a parent's place) left it, it carries interest for maintenance under the general law, the income is sufficient, and no rule of court says otherwise.
GIVEN `the legacy` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the legacy, in dollars
      `was it left by my parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was left by your parent or a person standing in the place of a parent (in loco parentis)
      `does it carry interest for my maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under the general law, the future or contingent legacy carries interest for your maintenance
      `is the income available sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the income available is sufficient to pay that interest
      `do rules of court set another rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a rule of court provides a different rate (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much interest does my parent's legacy carry` MEANS
    `s 37(3) -- the yearly interest my legacy carries` `the legacy` `was it left by my parent` `does it carry interest for my maintenance` `is the income available sufficient` `do rules of court set another rate`

§§ `Capital advanced for me (s 38)`

@export How much more of my trust capital may my trustee pay or use for my maintenance, education, advancement or benefit without the Court (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 38)? In all, up to $2000 or half the capital, whichever is greater (never more than the capital); more only with the Court's consent; nothing that prejudices a prior interest unless its holder consents in writing. What is advanced counts against your share.
GIVEN `am I entitled to the capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled (now or contingently, in possession or in remainder) to the capital of the trust property or a share of it
      `the capital of my share` IS A NUMBER @desc The capital of your share, before any amount was advanced under this section, in dollars
      `already advanced` IS A NUMBER @desc How much has already been paid or applied for you out of that capital under this section, in dollars
      `has the Court consented to more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has consented to a greater amount
      `would a prior interest be prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment would prejudice someone with a prior life or other prior interest (for example a parent entitled to the income for life)
      `has that person consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether that person exists, is of full age and has consented in writing
      `does the instrument say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will, deed or order creating the trust expresses a contrary intention (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much more of my capital may be advanced` MEANS
    `s 38 -- how much more of my capital may be advanced` `am I entitled to the capital` `the capital of my share` `already advanced` `has the Court consented to more` `would a prior interest be prejudiced` `has that person consented in writing` `does the instrument say otherwise`

§§ `Protective trusts (s 39)`

@export Who is my income held for under a protective trust (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 39)? For me during the trust period, until something happens (bankruptcy, an assignment, a charge) that would take it from me; then at the trustees' discretion for me and my spouse and issue, or, if I have none, for me and those who would take if I died.
GIVEN `is the trust period still running` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the period for which the income is held on protective trusts for you (your life or a shorter period) is still running
      `has something happened that would take the income from me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have done, attempted or suffered anything, or any event has happened, by which you would lose the right to the income if it were paid to you outright (bankruptcy, assigning or charging it, for example)
      `was it only an advance under a power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that was only an advance to you under a statutory or express power
      `do I have a spouse or issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a wife or husband, or children or more remote issue
GIVETH A `Who the protected income is held for`
`Who is my protected income held for` MEANS
    `s 39 -- who my protected income is held for` `is the trust period still running` `has something happened that would take the income from me` `was it only an advance under a power` `do I have a spouse or issue`

§§ `Replacing, adding and retiring trustees (Part III)`

@export Who may appoint a new trustee in place of my trustee (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 41(1) to (3), (9))? Where the trustee has died, been out of Victoria for more than a year without delegating, wants to be discharged, refuses, is unfit or incapable, is a minor, was removed under the trust's power, or is a dissolved company: the person the trust names to appoint, otherwise the continuing trustees (with leave if the trustee is a mental health patient with a beneficial interest).
GIVEN `what happened to my trustee` IS A `What has happened to my trustee` @desc What has happened to your trustee
      `the day my trustee left Victoria` IS A DATE @desc If your trustee is out of Victoria, the day they left (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `did my trustee properly delegate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your trustee is out of Victoria, whether they properly delegated the trust (by power of attorney under section 30)
      `is a nominated appointor able and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person the trust instrument names to appoint new trustees exists and is able and willing to act
      `is my trustee a patient with a beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your trustee is a patient under the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 and entitled in possession to a beneficial interest in the trust property
      `is my trustee a represented person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether your trustee has a guardian or administrator under the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019
GIVETH A `Who may appoint a replacement`
`Who may appoint a new trustee in place of mine` MEANS
    `s 41 -- who may appoint a replacement trustee` `what happened to my trustee` `the day my trustee left Victoria` `today` `did my trustee properly delegate` `is a nominated appointor able and willing` `is my trustee a patient with a beneficial interest` `is my trustee a represented person`

@export May additional trustees be appointed to my trust (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 41(6))? Where there are no more than three trustees and none is a trustee company, but never to more than four.
GIVEN `how many trustees now` IS A NUMBER @desc How many trustees the trust has now
      `is one a trustee company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of them is a trustee company
      `how many to add` IS A NUMBER @desc How many additional trustees would be appointed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May additional trustees be appointed` MEANS
    `s 41(6) -- additional trustees may be appointed` `how many trustees now` `is one a trustee company` `how many to add`

@export Is my trustee discharged without anyone replacing them (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 44)? Only if they declared in writing that they wish to be discharged, a trustee company or at least two individuals remain, the co-trustees and any appointor consent in writing, and any conveyance needed has been made.
GIVEN `did my trustee declare in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your trustee declared in writing that they wish to be discharged
      `how many individuals remain` IS A NUMBER @desc How many individuals will remain as trustees after the discharge
      `will a trustee company remain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a trustee company will remain as a trustee
      `did the others consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the co-trustees, and anyone empowered to appoint trustees, consented in writing to the discharge
      `has every needed conveyance been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any property that needs a conveyance to vest in the continuing trustees has been conveyed (yes if none needs one)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my trustee discharged without a replacement` MEANS
    `s 44 -- my trustee is discharged without a replacement` `did my trustee declare in writing` `how many individuals remain` `will a trustee company remain` `did the others consent in writing` `has every needed conveyance been made`

§§ `Asking the Court (Part IV)`

@export Can the Court appoint a new trustee of my trust on my application (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) ss 48, 64)? Yes where it is expedient and impracticable without the Court, and in particular where the trustee has been convicted on indictment, is a mental health patient, is bankrupt, or is a company in liquidation or dissolved.
GIVEN `am I beneficially interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are beneficially interested in the trust property (a beneficiary, including a child or a person under a disability)
      `the particular ground` IS A `Particular ground for the Court` @desc Whether your trustee has been convicted on indictment, is a patient under the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022, is bankrupt, or is a company in liquidation or dissolved, or none of these
      `is it expedient and impracticable without the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is expedient to appoint a new trustee and inexpedient, difficult or impracticable to do so without the Court (the Court's judgment; answer as you expect it to find)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Court appoint a new trustee on my application` MEANS
    `ss 48, 64 -- the Court may appoint a new trustee on my application` `am I beneficially interested` `the particular ground` `is it expedient and impracticable without the Court`

@export I am absolutely entitled to trust property and asked my trustee in writing to transfer it, collect its income or sue for it: has the trustee acted in time, or can I seek a vesting order (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 51(2)(i))? After 28 days' neglect or refusal following the written request, the Court may make a vesting order.
GIVEN `am I absolutely entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are absolutely entitled to the property (for example a beneficiary who has turned 18 and is entitled outright)
      `the day of my written request` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your written request to the trustee
      `has the trustee acted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee has done what you directed (conveyed the property, received its income, or sued for it)
      `the day the trustee acted` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it did (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE `What my written request led to`
`Has my trustee acted on my written request` MEANS
    `s 51(2)(i) -- what my written request led to` `am I absolutely entitled` `the day of my written request` `has the trustee acted` `the day the trustee acted` `today`

@export While I am a minor, can the Court make an order so that my trust property can be used for my maintenance, education, advancement or benefit (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 55)? Yes: it may appoint someone to transfer the property, or vest the right to transfer shares, collect income or sue for a debt.
GIVEN `my day of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `am I beneficially entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are beneficially entitled to the property (for example compensation or damages held on trust for you)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Court order my property be used for me while I am a minor` MEANS
    `s 55 -- the Court may make an order so my property can be used for me` `my day of birth` `today` `am I beneficially entitled`

@export Can I ask the Court to give my trustee a power it lacks for a transaction with the trust property (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 63)? Yes, where the transaction is expedient in the Court's opinion but the trustee has no power under the trust instrument or the law.
GIVEN `am I beneficially interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are beneficially interested under the trust
      `does the trustee lack the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee lacks the power for the transaction (a sale, lease, mortgage, purchase, investment, expenditure or other dealing) under the trust instrument and the law
      `would the Court find it expedient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court would consider the transaction expedient in managing or administering the trust property (the Court's judgment)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I ask the Court to give my trustee a power` MEANS
    `s 63 -- the Court may give the trustees the power on my application` `am I beneficially interested` `does the trustee lack the power` `would the Court find it expedient`

@export Can the Court approve an arrangement varying or revoking my trust on my behalf (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 63A)? For a minor or incapable beneficiary, a future member of a class, or an unborn person, only if it benefits that person; for a discretionary beneficiary under an intact protective trust, without that test. Not for property settled by Act of Parliament.
GIVEN `why the Court would act for me` IS A `Why the Court would approve for me` @desc Why the Court would approve on your behalf: you are a minor or incapable, may become entitled later as one of a class, would already be in that class now, are not yet born, have a discretionary interest under an intact protective trust, or are an adult able to assent yourself
      `would it benefit me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether carrying out the arrangement would be for your benefit (the Court's judgment)
      `was the property settled by Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trust property was settled by an Act of Parliament
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Court approve a variation of my trust for me` MEANS
    `s 63A -- the Court may approve the variation on my behalf` `why the Court would act for me` `would it benefit me` `was the property settled by Act of Parliament`

@export Can the Court excuse my trustee, wholly or partly, from personal liability for a breach of trust (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 67)? Only if the trustee acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused.
GIVEN `did my trustee act honestly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your trustee acted honestly
      `did my trustee act reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your trustee acted reasonably
      `ought my trustee fairly to be excused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your trustee ought fairly to be excused for the breach and for not asking the Court for directions (the Court's judgment)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Court excuse my trustee` MEANS
    `s 67 -- the Court may relieve my trustee from personal liability` `did my trustee act honestly` `did my trustee act reasonably` `ought my trustee fairly to be excused`

@export Can the Court take my interest in the trust to indemnify my trustee for a breach of trust (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 68)? Yes, where the trustee committed the breach at my instigation or request, or with my written consent.
GIVEN `did I instigate it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee committed the breach at your instigation
      `did I request it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee committed it at your request
      `did I consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consented to it in writing (consent not in writing does not count)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my interest be impounded for the trustee's breach` MEANS
    `s 68 -- the Court may impound my interest to indemnify the trustee` `did I instigate it` `did I request it` `did I consent in writing`

@export Can my trustees pay the trust money into court (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 69)? The trustees, or a majority of them, may pay it into the Supreme Court; if the others will not concur, the Court may order payment by the majority. The receipt discharges the trustees.
GIVEN `how many trustees` IS A NUMBER @desc How many trustees the trust has
      `how many want to pay in` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them want to pay the money or securities into court
      `do the others concur` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the others concur
GIVETH A MAYBE `How the money may go into court`
`Can my trustees pay the trust money into court` MEANS
    `s 69 -- how the trust money may be paid into court` `how many trustees` `how many want to pay in` `do the others concur`

§§ `Commission (s 77)`

@export What is the most commission the Court can allow my trustee out of the trust funds (Trustee Act 1958 (Vic) s 77)? Up to five per cent, as is just and reasonable, for the trustee of a settlement.
GIVEN `is my trustee the trustee of a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your trustee is the trustee of a settlement (a trust created by deed or will)
      `the amount it is reckoned on` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the commission is reckoned on, in dollars (the Act does not say on what: for example the trust funds or the income received)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most commission my trustee can be allowed` MEANS
    `s 77 -- the most commission the Court may allow` `is my trustee the trustee of a settlement` `the amount it is reckoned on`
